Privacy Policy for Daily Usage

Effective Date: May 22, 2026

This Privacy Policy describes how Google AdMob and the app Daily Usage (“the App”) handles information when you use our mobile application.

1. Information About the App

App Name: Daily Usage
Package Name: com.app.daily_usage
Developer: Pranay Prajapati
Support Email: pranay.prajapati.86@gmail.com

Daily Usage is an application that helps users manage daily stock usage, purchases, and remaining inventory. Users can add, edit, and delete item lists and track stock usage locally on their device.

2. Information Collection and Use

Daily Usage does not collect, store, or share any personal information from users.

All app data, including item lists and stock records, is stored locally on the user’s device only.

We do not:

Require user registration
Collect personal data
Store data on external servers
Share user data with third parties
3. Local Data Storage

The App stores user-created data locally on the device to provide core functionality such as:

Managing item lists
Tracking stock purchases
Calculating stock usage and remaining quantity

This data never leaves the user’s device unless the user manually backs up or transfers their device data using their own device tools.

4. Advertising

The App uses Google AdMob to display advertisements.

AdMob may collect and process certain data automatically, such as:

Device information
Advertising ID
IP address
App interaction information

This information is handled according to Google’s own privacy policies.

You can learn more here:

Google Privacy Policy
How Google Uses Information From Apps
5. Permissions

Daily Usage does not request sensitive device permissions.

6. Children’s Privacy

Daily Usage is not directed toward children under the age of 13.

We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.

7. Data Deletion

Since all data is stored locally on the user’s device:

Users can delete app data at any time by:
Clearing app storage from device settings, or
Uninstalling the application

No user data is stored on external servers.

8. Security

Because all data is stored locally on the device, users are responsible for maintaining the security of their own device.

We do not transmit or store user data online.

9. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected by updating the “Effective Date” at the top of this document.

Users are encouraged to review this Privacy Policy periodically.

